6. The mechanism: G_{g,p,11}(w) = -[G^F_{g,p}(w + 1/2) + G^F_{g,1-p}(w - 1/2)] / 2w
 So the bottom (at w = H - 1/2) and top (at w = H + 1/2) of one Dirac pole have weights in the
 ratio (H + 1/2) : -(H - 1/2), which is what lets the super-centre integral collapse them.
